WARNING:AVOID_EXTERNS: externs should be avoided in .c files
#272: FILE: mm/memcontrol.c:1242:
+	struct dirty_info uninitialized_var(cur_info);

Function prototypes don't need to be declared extern in .h
files.  It's assumed by the compiler and is unnecessary.

WARNING:FUNCTION_ARGUMENTS: function definition argument 'cur_info' should also have an identifier name
#272: FILE: mm/memcontrol.c:1242:
+	struct dirty_info uninitialized_var(cur_info);

This warning is emitted due to any of the following reasons:

  1. Arguments for the function declaration do not follow
     the identifier name.  Example::

       void foo
       (int bar, int baz)

     This should be corrected to::

       void foo(int bar, int baz)

  2. Some arguments for the function definition do not
     have an identifier name.  Example::

       void foo(int)

     All arguments should have identifier names.

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'info->nr_writeback == ULONG_MAX'
#300: FILE: mm/memcontrol.c:1270:
+		if ((info->nr_writeback == ULONG_MAX) ||
+		    (cur_info.dirty_thresh - usage <
+		     info->dirty_thresh - dirty_info_reclaimable(info) -
+		     info->nr_writeback))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

WARNING:AVOID_BUG: Avoid crashing the kernel - try using WARN_ON & recovery code rather than BUG() or BUG_ON()
#349: FILE: mm/memcontrol.c:1319:
+		BUG();

BUG() or BUG_ON() should be avoided totally.
Use WARN() and WARN_ON() instead, and handle the "impossible"
error condition as gracefully as possible.

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/deprecated.html#bug-and-bug-on

